# ceralive-slot-sync.exclude — rsync --exclude-from list for
# /usr/libexec/ceralive/ceralive-slot-sync (task 26).
#
# Installed verbatim to /usr/lib/ceralive/slot-sync.exclude. These are runtime,
# ephemeral or download-cache paths that must never be mirrored between slots:
# neither slot's own transient state belongs on the other slot, and copying it
# would make the mirror non-deterministic across runs for no benefit.
#
# /dev/* is excluded here too, matching /proc, /sys and /run — but the caller
# ADMITS a handful of conventional static device special files ahead of this
# file on the rsync command line (--include=/dev/null etc., see
# ceralive-slot-sync.sh's header comment for why a plain --exclude-from file
# cannot express that override itself). Do not add a static-node name here:
# add it as an --include on the command line, in front of --exclude-from.
#
# /data is NOT listed here. It is intentionally never touched by this list
# because it is not part of either rootfs slot's tree at all — it is a THIRD,
# already-shared partition mounted at runtime (see docs/partition-contract.md),
# so it never appears under the bind-mounted "/" this script rsyncs from in the
# first place. Do not add a redundant /data/* entry.
/var/cache/apt/archives/*
/tmp/*
/var/tmp/*
/run/*
/proc/*
/sys/*
/dev/*
/lost+found
